      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transport from Chittoor</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Transporting a two‑wheeler from Chittoor to Hyderabad involves a few non‑negotiable documents that ensure a smooth hand‑over to the logistics provider and protect you against loss or damage. Below is a concise checklist of the paperwork you must prepare before the bike leaves your doorstep.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self‑attested RC (Registration Certificate) photocopy</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A clear copy of the original RC, signed and attested by you, serves as proof of ownership. The logistics partner will verify the details against the bike’s chassis number.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC (Pollution Under Control) certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The latest emission test report, dated within the last three months, is required to confirm that the vehicle complies with environmental norms. Some carriers may refuse transport of a bike without a valid PUC.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid insurance certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The existing third‑party liability policy (or a comprehensive cover) must be active at the time of dispatch. Provide a photocopy of the policy page that lists the bike’s registration number and the insurer’s contact details.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑approved consignment bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Indian Bike Association (IBA) issues a standardized consignment note that records the shipper, consignee, bike specifications, and agreed freight charges. This bilty is signed by both the sender and the transport agency and acts as the legal contract for the movement of the bike.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>In addition to the mandatory documents, it is highly advisable to secure a <strong>100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong>. This policy covers the full market value of the bike against risks such as theft, accidental damage, fire, or natural calamities during the entire journey.</p>
<p>The insurer will require the bike’s invoice or a valuation report, and the premium is typically calculated as a small percentage of the declared value. Opting for full‑value coverage eliminates any financial surprise should an unfortunate event occur while the bike is in transit.</p>

<p>Once you have gathered the self‑attested RC, current PUC, insurance certificate, and the IBA‑approved bilty, hand them over to the transport agency at the point of pickup. Verify that the carrier’s driver signs the consignment bilty and that a copy of the marine insurance policy is attached.</p>
<p>With these documents in order, your bike will be legally compliant, well‑protected, and ready for a hassle‑free move from Chittoor to Hyderabad.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



